Provider JSON files contain every price tuple from src/generated/model-metadata.ts,
which is generated by scripts/generate-model-metadata.ts from the bundled
scripts/model-metadata.source.json. Non-price metadata is omitted.
rules.json contains the complete expected-price overlays, verified corrections,
provider aliases, vendor lookup order, priority multipliers, and context tiers
from src/usage/expected-prices.ts and src/generated/model-metadata.ts.
Source URLs and verification dates are preserved per rule. These are pinned
reference estimates, not claims that present-day vendor billing matches them.

The Go normalization, resolution, cache write, and tier algorithms are adapted
from src/usage/cost.ts and related provider identity helpers at that revision.
Original MIT terms remain applicable to the adapted material; new repository
implementation is licensed under Apache-2.0.

Regenerate with Node.js 24:
node packages/tairouter/pricing/generate.mjs /path/to/clean/pinned/opencodex
The generator verifies the revision and refuses a modified source checkout.
No runtime network price updates are performed.

testdata/*.json contains differential fixtures generated by executing the pinned
src/usage/cost.ts estimator with empty deployment configuration. Fixtures retain
its price attribution and are covered by the same MIT notice. They cover all
expected-price rows, context thresholds, priority rules, Cursor variants and
Antigravity aliases. They do not assert live vendor/account verification.
